<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 586 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 586 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of September 12 raised 586 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 435 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 234 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.61 (14.61)	    67.4  (104.6)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.92 (16.92)	   108   (82.8)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.80 (17.85)	   118.2   (73.9)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.74 (21.76)	   292.4  (173.8)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,560 to the U.S. dollar on Monday, unchanged from last week. It closed at 1,612.5 one year ago.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056 645456</p>
